      "content": "It's great that you want to map your intuitive insights to actual data for a predictive model. To do this, start by recording the details of each intuitive \"spike\" you experience, including the time, context, and specific predictions made. For each instance, log the relevant data points (e.g., stock prices, weather conditions, people’s actions) to see if there's a pattern.\n\nTo structure your dataset, create a spreadsheet with columns for the timestamp of the intuitive spike, the intuition experienced, and the corresponding real-world data before, during, and after the event. Plotting these on a timeline may reveal trends or correlations. Over time, you can use statistical methods to analyze the dataset and refine the structure to improve your predictive model's accuracy. Remember to consider external variables that might influence these events to avoid skewed results.",
